**Current phase, 2026-11-15:** finish source-only removal of known unnecessary work, reconcile the plan, then return. No tests, compilation, measurements, shipping, installation or reboot in this phase.

**Latest source reconciliation, 2026-11-16:** identity-first focus lookup and shared immutable target observations, selective saved-focus restoration, and requested-ID dialog-placement preparation are implemented. FOCUS-TARGET-VERIFY, FOCUS-RESTORATION-VERIFY and TRANSIENT-PLACEMENT-VERIFY own their unrun checks. Earlier root-scope, preference, inheritance, validation, geometry/solver, command/device settings, opening/reference, shared controls, input, canvas, feature and backend families retain verification rather than coding tasks. P124 remains wider inventory/coverage. Current source/ownership checks, deferred retries and required model writes remain; further reductions must name actual repeated or unused work rather than weakening those requirements.

[Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) is the single current implementation and acceptance report. Its source-only receipts describe the current candidate; its remaining obligations order later evaluation by the worst responsiveness/resource failures. This native index preserves P identities and conditional research constraints, not a competing instruction to reimplement every older idea.

Completed measurement coverage, real system attribution, mixed-route repair, local-edit attribution, retained panels and surface fingerprint lookups are removed from this queue. The obsolete duplicate-ELF task is also retired because the current measurement archive omits that payload. Their stable Records are evidence chapters. Source-only implementations stay at quantity zero as **verification** tasks; implementation is not proof of a gain.

**Next authorized execution phase:** verify the complete source batch, first the short-title save/backlog and populated-reveal failures, then mixed input, quiet settling, graphics completion and the physical daily desktop. Preserve all mandatory Protein/glyph/edit-panel checks. The current instruction does not authorize that execution yet.

**Conditional follow-ups:** unimplemented proposals below require evidence after the batch. They are not known defects merely because a previous plan suggested an index, cache, worker, virtual list or new representation. Full viewport virtualization, broader main/render overlap, alternate style storage, reaction detachment and transaction coalescing remain unproved. Preserve semantic/authority/durability/resource boundaries; do not revive rejected alternatives unchanged. Delivery cleanup and compiler experiments stay deferred.

The old sync/history/Karma delegation is historical coordination, not evidence of an active owner or a completed fix. Inspect current changes before any overlapping work. Current runtime acceptance remains open even where a private implementation check passed.

